{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block content %}
<section class="dest-hero"><div class="wrap narrow">
  <h1>Mexican peso converter</h1>
  <p class="lede">Convert between pesos and US dollars, Canadian dollars, euros and pounds using a live market rate.</p>
  <form class="panel form mt5" id="fx-tool" onsubmit="return false">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="field"><label for="fx-amt">Amount</label><input id="fx-amt" type="number" min="0" step="any" value="100"></div>
      <div class="field"><label for="fx-from">From</label><select id="fx-from"><option>USD</option><option>CAD</option><option>EUR</option><option>GBP</option><option>MXN</option></select></div>
    </div>
    <div class="field"><label for="fx-to">To</label><select id="fx-to"><option>MXN</option><option>USD</option><option>CAD</option><option>EUR</option><option>GBP</option></select></div>
    <p style="font-size:1.6rem;font-weight:800" id="fx-res" aria-live="polite">{% if fx.rates %}100 USD = {{ '{:,.2f}'.format(fx.rates.MXN * 100) }} MXN{% endif %}</p>
    <p class="small mb0" id="fx-stamp">Rate snapshot · {{ fx.date }}</p>
  </form>
</div></section>
<section class="band-tight"><div class="wrap narrow prose">
  <h2>Money tips for Mexico</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Pay in pesos.</b> When a card machine offers to charge you in your home currency, decline; the conversion rate is almost always worse.</li>
    <li><b>Use bank ATMs inside branches or malls</b> and choose "decline conversion" on screen. Withdraw larger amounts less often to limit fees.</li>
    <li><b>Carry small notes.</b> Taxis, markets, cenotes and tips often need cash, and change for big notes can be scarce.</li>
    <li><b>Tipping:</b> 10-15% in restaurants is normal; a few dollars a day for housekeeping and small tips for guides and drivers are appreciated.</li>
    <li><b>Airport exchange counters</b> have the weakest rates; change only what you need for the first taxi.</li>
  </ul>
</div></section>
{% endblock %}
